                # So the count is (d) choose (l-1) * (d) ? Wait, no
                # Wait, the remaining digits can be any digits less than d, but they can be in any order
                # So for each of the l-1 digits, there are d choices (0 to d-1)
                # But since digits can be repeated, the number is d^(l-1)
                # Wait, but the first digit is d, and the rest can be any digits less than d
